# Citation metadata (Citation File Format 1.2.0).
#
# GitHub reads this file and renders a "Cite this repository" button in the
# sidebar, which offers APA and BibTeX. Zenodo and the CFF tooling read the same
# file, so the version and release date below must track the actual release;
# tests/test_docs_and_community_health.py holds them to `packetiq.__version__`
# and to the newest CHANGELOG entry so this cannot quietly go stale.
#
# No contact address is published here on purpose: `pyproject.toml` declares the
# author by name only, and this file keeps that posture. Add an `email:` line
# under `authors` if you want one on the citation.
cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use PacketIQ in academic or published work, please cite it as below."
type: software
title: "PacketIQ: an offline-first network forensics and SOC triage platform with deterministic output grounding"
abstract: >-
  PacketIQ is a defensive network forensics platform for SOC analysts, threat
  hunters and incident responders. It ingests packet captures, Zeek conn.log
  files, NetFlow and IPFIX exports, or a live interface, and produces an
  evidence-backed analysis: 18 detection types across 12 detector modules,
  enrichment against verbatim snapshots of public OSINT threat-intelligence
  feeds, attack-chain correlation mapped to MITRE ATT&CK and the
  Lockheed Martin kill chain, and deployable output as pySigma-valid SIGMA
  rules, STIX 2.1 bundles, MISP events and evidence PCAP slices. Threat-actor
  output is reported as behavioural TTP overlap rather than confirmed
  attribution. An optional LLM copilot is constrained by a deterministic
  post-generation grounding filter that redacts every entity absent from the
  evidence the model was given, which holds entity hallucination at zero
  independently of the model used.
authors:
  - family-names: Kumar
    given-names: Jatin
    affiliation: "Birmingham City University"
version: 1.1.0
date-released: "2026-11-15"
license: MIT
repository-code: "https://github.com/Jatinkumar78/PacketIQ"
url: "https://github.com/Jatinkumar78/PacketIQ"
keywords:
  - network forensics
  - intrusion detection
  - packet capture
  - pcap
  - threat intelligence
  - MITRE ATT&CK
  - SIGMA
  - STIX
  - digital forensics and incident response
  - security operations centre
  - large language models
  - hallucination mitigation

# The methods write-up that accompanies the grounding guardrail. It is a short
# paper held in this repository at docs/paper/deterministic_output_grounding.md
# and has no venue, DOI or publisher, so none is claimed here.
preferred-citation:
  type: report
  title: "Deterministic Output Grounding: A Post-Generation Guarantee Against Entity Hallucination in LLM Security Copilots"
  authors:
    - family-names: Kumar
      given-names: Jatin
      affiliation: "Birmingham City University"
  institution:
    name: "Birmingham City University"
  year: 2026
  url: "https://github.com/Jatinkumar78/PacketIQ/blob/main/docs/paper/deterministic_output_grounding.md"
